* sg13g2-pll :: sim/sg13cmos5l-postlayout-pex-pvt (issue #102, Part of #16)
* POST-LAYOUT PFD transient -- the parasitic-annotated twin of
* ../../sg13cmos5l-closed-loop-lock/testbench/tb_pfd_only.sp.tmpl, kept
* line-for-line comparable to it so the only difference between the two
* arms' numbers is the extracted interconnect R/C.
*
* Same stimulus, same averaging window, same .meas lines as that campaign's
* own PFD-only diagnostic: two pulse trains sharing one period/high-time,
* only the START DELAY differs, so the REF/FB edges keep the same lead/lag
* relationship every cycle and a steady-state UP/DN duty-cycle reading is
* available from a short transient. `up_avg`/`dn_avg` are averaged over
* [@TAVG0@, @TSTOP@] -- the first four reference cycles (startup/reset
* transient) are skipped, exactly as that script's own TAVG0 does.
*
* The DUT is `pll_pfd`, the subcircuit `klt extract --deck sg13cmos5l
* --parasitics --pdk ihp-sg13cmos5l` produced from the same routed GDS as
* Matrices A/B (layout record 20260830-204105-457cf5b): 66 devices, 37
* nets, 264 parasitic resistors and 37 substrate + 543 coupling capacitors.
* This is one of the three blocks ../lvs-recheck/summary.json confirms
* LVS-MATCHES its schematic (66/66 devices, 37/37 nets), so a deviation
* measured here is attributable to the extracted parasitics, not to an
* unverified layout-vs-schematic topology.
*
* ../run_pfd.sh substitutes @CORNER_MOS@ (cornerMOShv.lib), @TEMP@ (degC),
* @VDD@ (V), @TREF@/@TREFH@ (period / high time of both pulse trains, s),
* @REF_DELAY@/@FB_DELAY@ (s -- exactly one is 0, the other is the fixed
* per-cycle lead/lag under test), @TSTOP@, @TPRINT@, @TMAX@, @TAVG0@, and
* @PFD_PEX_DUT@/@PFD_PEX_INST@ (the pex-to-ngspice.py-rewritten netlist and
* the make-inst.py-generated instantiation -- pin order derived from the
* extracted cell's own .SUBCKT pin list, never transcribed by hand) plus
* @PDK_ROOT@/@PDK@ (ngspice's .lib/.include parser does not expand
* environment variables, issue #54).
*
* The extracted netlist declares its own `.GLOBAL vsubs` and ties it to
* ground only through klt's 1e12-ohm DC tie; every extracted net-to-ground
* parasitic capacitor returns to that node, so -- exactly like
* tb_cp_dc_pex.sp.tmpl -- it is held hard at 0 V rather than left floating.

.lib @PDK_ROOT@/@PDK@/libs.tech/ngspice/models/cornerMOShv.lib @CORNER_MOS@
.option scale=1 temp=@TEMP@

.include @PFD_PEX_DUT@
.include @PFD_PEX_INST@

Vdd_pfd vdd_pfd 0 dc @VDD@
Vsubs vsubs 0 dc 0

* Both pulse trains share one period/high-time; only the START DELAY differs
* between REF and FB, so the two edges keep the SAME lead/lag relationship
* every single cycle (a fixed phase offset, not a frequency difference).
Vref ref 0 pulse(0 @VDD@ @REF_DELAY@ 100p 100p @TREFH@ @TREF@)
Vfb  fb  0 pulse(0 @VDD@ @FB_DELAY@  100p 100p @TREFH@ @TREF@)

.tran @TPRINT@ @TSTOP@ 0 @TMAX@

.control
run
meas tran up_avg avg v(up) from=@TAVG0@ to=@TSTOP@
meas tran dn_avg avg v(dn) from=@TAVG0@ to=@TSTOP@
print up_avg dn_avg
.endc
.end
